      "content": "yeah exactly. it feels like the \"pro-trade\" side always talks about stuff like \"comparative advantage\" and \"global productivity\" but those just sound like buzzwords to justify letting corporations run the show. if the trade-off is basically destroying the middle class in developed nations just to shave a few cents off a plastic toy, isn't it pretty obvious that the current system of globalist trade deals is fundamentally broken?",
